Tool call input: {'code': 'import requests, xml.etree.ElementTree as ET
pmid='25423132'
r=requests.get('https://eutils.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/entrez/eutils/efetch.fcgi',params={'db':'pubmed','id':pmid,'retmode':'xml'},timeout=30)
root=ET.fromstring(r.text)
for tag in ['ArticleTitle','AbstractText','Journal','PubDate','AuthorList']:
    if tag=='AbstractText':
        vals=[('' if x.text is None else x.text) for x in root.findall('.//AbstractText')]
        print('ABSTRACT:\n'+'\n'.join(vals))
    elif tag=='ArticleTitle': print('TITLE:', ''.join(root.find('.//ArticleTitle').itertext()))
    elif tag=='Journal': print('JOURNAL:', ''.join(root.find('.//Journal/Title').itertext()))
    elif tag=='PubDate': print('DATE:', ' '.join(root.find('.//PubDate').itertext()))
    elif tag=='AuthorList': print('AUTHORS:', ', '.join(' '.join(a.itertext()) for a in root.findall('.//AuthorList/Author')))
print('DOI:', [x.text for x in root.findall('.//ArticleId[@IdType="doi"]')])', 'language': 'python'}

The direct PubMed record answers the question: in C6 rat glioma cells, GDNF increased β-catenin Tyr-654 phosphorylation and increased cytoplasmic/nuclear phospho-β-catenin, with immunocytochemical evidence of nuclear translocation. I will now check the evidence graph for duplicates before recording this finding.

